I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T15:15:43-08:00","id":86302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=86085#post86085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I have one question. Does Mortal Remains have any rules update for The Code?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing as this is the book to update Hunter to GMC, I would certainly expect something for it. After all, Morality is now Integrity and the Code was what altered Morality. Off the top of my head, that's the biggest mechanic to update - unless they go through each individual power from the core book and update all of them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T17:59:00-08:00","id":86390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=86085#post86085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I have one question. Does Mortal Remains have any rules update for The Code?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. I didn't have space to rehash the Code appendix in entirety. Mind you this isn't actually the Hunter equivalent of Blood &amp; Smoke or Idigam Chronicle. It's some patch notes to make the rules work together. It's a pretty short section, all things considered. Hunters can use Trigger Points with Integrity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T18:08:56-08:00","id":86394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=86390#post86390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really. I didn't have space to rehash the Code appendix in entirety. Mind you this isn't actually the Hunter equivalent of Blood &amp; Smoke or Idigam Chronicle. It's some patch notes to make the rules work together. It's a pretty short section, all things considered. Hunters can use Trigger Points with Integrity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possible addition: you get to change one Breaking Point per violation of Integrity with the Code, and it causes the Trigger Point. Not something to put in the book, but possible errata?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T00:59:19-08:00","id":86576,"title":"","content":"That's all I needed to know. Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T04:48:01-08:00","id":86678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=86390#post86390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really. I didn't have space to rehash the Code appendix in entirety. Mind you this isn't actually the Hunter equivalent of Blood &amp; Smoke or Idigam Chronicle. It's some patch notes to make the rules work together. It's a pretty short section, all things considered. Hunters can use Trigger Points with Integrity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I'm totally absolutely wrong hahaha so what is that section comprised of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T05:00:05-08:00","id":86680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=86678#post86678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh. I'm totally absolutely wrong hahaha so what is that section comprised of?</div> </div> </div> </div>Updated rules for risking Willpower.<br /> <br /> A couple of adaptation notes for Endowments.<br /> <br /> Couple of notes on Dread Powers. S<br /> <br /> ome notes on updating Merits, including things like how to reconcile Safe House with Safe Place.<br /> <br /> Updated Compact and Conspiracy Status rules reflecting the new Merits, and a few semantic notes.<br /> <br /> Rules for Beats and &quot;Practical Beats&quot; that the cell earns. Minor notes on how to use Tactics with the new rules, as well as integrating Beats with them.<br /> <br /> I added a section on creating monsters, it's pretty rough but offers some ideas and advice.<br /> <br /> Then I offer some loose creation rules for less important and more important monsters (so you don't need to fully stat every mook).<br /> <br /> There's some guidelines for creating new monster templates whole cloth.<br /> <br /> There's a new monster Potency trait to help the rules mesh better with the various game lines.<br /> <br /> Potency also adds to any rolls against the monster that utilize their bans/flaws.<br /> <br /> There are examples of what Potency means for some common monster types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T10:20:31-08:00","id":86842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=86680#post86680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Updated Compact and Conspiracy Status rules reflecting the new Merits, and a few semantic notes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will C&amp;C Status use the same rules for what you can get at each dot as Mystery Cult Initiation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T11:31:35-08:00","id":86894,"title":"","content":"It sounds like there's still room for a Hunter Chronicle Update book, then...maybe featuring Slashers as the antagonist, so they can be updated too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T11:55:05-08:00","id":86910,"title":"","content":"My vote would be for Cults. Since that leads to organisation vs organisation rather than a group of hunters vs a lone Slasher, and can work with both purely mortal &quot;evil-hunter-like&quot; antagonists and a cult run by a monster. Plus when you get down to it all Slashers have a motivation of &quot;kill X&quot;, cults have more verity.<br /> <br /> The only reason I'm not reworking Cults to do so is that it's a lot of work and I'm one person, and also I wouldn't have much idea how to balance the core 12's chronicle rewrite with the core 12's views on cults","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 03-08-2014, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T18:32:55-08:00","id":87128,"title":"","content":"Updating slashers at the same time is kind of low-hanging fruit; they were introduced as Hunter antagonists when Hunter rolled out, they also risk willpower, Undertakings could probably interact with the Condition/Beat system somehow, etc. <br /> <br /> I feel like cult and cult organization rules are broadly applicable, better suited to a World of Darkness book that brought an elaborated Mummy-style cult system to everybody. <br /> <br /> A lot of the Endowments and Tactics could use a reworking, just...generally. I think the Aegis Kai Doru need a revamping with the recognition that &quot;Relic&quot; is a merit anyone can basically take, and &quot;has a magic item&quot; is too broadly applicable a character concept to sustain a conspiracy's big trick. <br /> <br /> I'd envision giving them something else, and opening up Relic as an endowment any tier of hunter can take - &quot;General Endowments&quot;, say. Could also be used to model low-level ritual magic with a Blood Sorcery -style system for the &quot;Ritual&quot; endowment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T18:37:17-08:00","id":87135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=86842#post86842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Will C&amp;C Status use the same rules for what you can get at each dot as Mystery Cult Initiation?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I was going to do that, but I came to the realization that as a supplement, this isn't really a core update, and if I do the core ones, I'm omitting all the great ones from the various supplements. <br /> <br /> And yes, there's plenty of room for a Chronicle book. If, hypothetically, I were to pitch to do one, I probably wouldn't go with slashers or cults. I would definitely, hypothetically, go for something that screams &quot;monster,&quot; not just messed up human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T20:45:40-08:00","id":87186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=87135#post87135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. I was going to do that, but I came to the realization that as a supplement, this isn't really a core update, and if I do the core ones, I'm omitting all the great ones from the various supplements.<br /> <br /> And yes, there's plenty of room for a Chronicle book. If, hypothetically, I were to pitch to do one, I probably wouldn't go with slashers or cults. I would definitely, hypothetically, go for something that screams &quot;monster,&quot; not just messed up human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something like &quot;anything in the night&quot;? It's pretty much hunters versus the entire world.(Grossly exaggerated)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T22:46:59-08:00","id":87255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=87186#post87186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something like &quot;anything in the night&quot;? It's pretty much hunters versus the entire world.(Grossly exaggerated)</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of us reaaaaaaaally want a book that covers the Vigil across the world (think the H:tV version of &quot;Rage Across the World&quot;). I think a worldwide-spanning story about the hunt would be great for a chronicle book; would definitely consider help funding it on Kickstarter. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T22:57:31-08:00","id":87263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=87255#post87255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some of us reaaaaaaaally want a book that covers the Vigil across the world (think the H:tV version of &quot;Rage Across the World&quot;). I think a worldwide-spanning story about the hunt would be great for a chronicle book; would definitely consider help funding it on Kickstarter. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>One thing all the Chronicle books is doing is highlighting various places around the world, and how the game might come into play there. If we ever did a Hunter book, it'd have a similar section. <br /> <br /> A thing worth noting is, if you liked Tokyo in Blood &amp; Smoke, I recently got greenlit to include a Tokyo section in Idigam Chronicle and Fallen World Chronicle. If I get my way, I'm going to turn it into a sort of cosmopolitan setting book like Chicago, spread over the various Chronicles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T01:13:06-08:00","id":87343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=87135#post87135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, there's plenty of room for a Chronicle book. If, hypothetically, I were to pitch to do one, I probably wouldn't go with slashers or cults. I would definitely, hypothetically, go for something that screams &quot;monster,&quot; not just messed up human.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're interested I'd love to debate the merits of cults vs something-screams-monster with you? You've made a lot of great decisions and I'd like to see what I'm not seeing about the other options. <br /> <br /> The reason I think cults are appropriate is two fold: Diversity and Scalability.<br /> <br /> Firstly diversity, Hunter has always put the ability to play hunters vs any other WoD gameline as a core feature and I think making a specific type of monster into a strixx like core focus could detract from that. Cults on the other hand can, more or less, tie into every gameline. Vampires and Mages lead cults of mortals. Cults can worship Spirits or True Fae. Etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> Secondly scalability. With cults you can increase the supernatural ability of the cultists/cult leaders independently of the cult's mundane resources like size, influence and wealth. For most monsters the two are a bit more linked (Vampires use their mental powers to acquire resources, and even if they don't a fledgling vampire has significantly more supernatural power than Ron Hubbard)<br /> <br /> I think that this kind of flexibility will be great for a core opponent because Hunters tend to grow massively in social/organisational power but hardly at all in personal/supernatural power. As a core-focus Cults would provide opportunities to get really let loose and show what happens when the Catholic Church gets proof that the international Cult of Dagon is sacrafacing virgins and decides its time to end them, but you can also use cults as a lead-in to the classic hunter story where the cult reappears with new members everywhere that True Fae does, so a group of mortals have to go into a gunfight with a vastly superior supernatural foe.<br /> <br /> I think that the way you can scale cults to each tier - in the same ways that hunters scale at each tier - or use them as a lead in to monsters that scale in entirely different ways really makes cults shine as a hunter antagonist.<br /> <br /> The fact cults can be seen as a dark mirror of hunters is just the icing on the cake.<br /> <br /> <br /> So that's why I'm pro cults, if you're willing please enlighten me to what awesome advantages that thing-that-screams monster has that I'm not seeing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T01:45:52-08:00","id":87370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=87343#post87343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're interested I'd love to debate the merits of cults vs something-screams-monster with you? You've made a lot of great decisions and I'd like to see what I'm not seeing about the other options.<br /> <br /> The reason I think cults are appropriate is two fold: Diversity and Scalability.<br /> <br /> Firstly diversity, Hunter has always put the ability to play hunters vs any other WoD gameline as a core feature and I think making a specific type of monster into a strixx like core focus could detract from that. Cults on the other hand can, more or less, tie into every gameline. Vampires and Mages lead cults of mortals. Cults can worship Spirits or True Fae. Etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> Secondly scalability. With cults you can increase the supernatural ability of the cultists/cult leaders independently of the cult's mundane resources like size, influence and wealth. For most monsters the two are a bit more linked (Vampires use their mental powers to acquire resources, and even if they don't a fledgling vampire has significantly more supernatural power than Ron Hubbard)<br /> <br /> I think that this kind of flexibility will be great for a core opponent because Hunters tend to grow massively in social/organisational power but hardly at all in personal/supernatural power. As a core-focus Cults would provide opportunities to get really let loose and show what happens when the Catholic Church gets proof that the international Cult of Dagon is sacrafacing virgins and decides its time to end them, but you can also use cults as a lead-in to the classic hunter story where the cult reappears with new members everywhere that True Fae does, so a group of mortals have to go into a gunfight with a vastly superior supernatural foe.<br /> <br /> I think that the way you can scale cults to each tier - in the same ways that hunters scale at each tier - or use them as a lead in to monsters that scale in entirely different ways really makes cults shine as a hunter antagonist.<br /> <br /> The fact cults can be seen as a dark mirror of hunters is just the icing on the cake.<br /> <br /> <br /> So that's why I'm pro cults, if you're willing please enlighten me to what awesome advantages that thing-that-screams monster has that I'm not seeing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Mind you, I don't have a TON of time, so if I back away or post slowly, understand that I'm facing some intense deadlines right now. I'll read it regardless. <br /> <br /> The short end of it is: <br /> <br /> 1) I think cults are mostly comprised of victims, and I don't really want to do a game about stopping and ostensibly killing victims. <br /> <br /> 2) Cults tend to imply the existence of bigger things. We could do God-Machine cults, but I feel like those have a better place in Demon. They could be big Lovecraftian entities, but I don't really get much out of those. <br /> <br /> 3) I think monsters serve as a really good anchoring point for &quot;what is a monster, and what is human?&quot; debates. When hunters default to hunting clear monsters, that gives them a strong foundation that justifies what they do. But then when they move into other territory as an exception, they have to reconcile that as an exception, handling each as a case-by-case situation. <br /> <br /> 4) I like hunters being definitely the underdogs, needing tactics, compromise, and attrition to win their battles. Big inhuman scary things work well with that. <br /> <br /> 5) I think that killing cultists removes a lot of the gray areas from Hunter. While not all Hunter characters would resort to killing, it'd be a standard for at least some of the Hunter groups. And I find that to be pretty irreconcilably wrong. <br /> <br /> 6) When I think of Hunter, I think of hunting monsters. Cultists aren't monsters. So there's a cognitive disconnect. <br /> <br /> 7) Cults tend to have an &quot;othering&quot; element to them. It's one of my big gripes with Lovecraft. While I don't think it'd be a huge problem with my writers, I think it'd be an easy thing to fall back on. I don't want to see another WoD: Gypsies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T04:53:23-07:00","id":87427,"title":"","content":"You make some very good points <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The morality/theme ones particularly, it didn't really occur to me before how making cultists the default enemy could skew the perceived morality/themes of hunters. I guess it's because I consider a lot of the monster splats to be victims and because I don't like species as a justification for murder and would hold a morality system that can be applied consistently to humans and monsters as the ideal Hunter code (it would have to include something like fair trials where possible of course) - but I acknowledge that you're completely correct. Even if the writing intentionally tries to soften the blow, making the primary enemy humans will be a major change in tone, and not for the the better.<br /> <br /> The one I strongly disagree with is number 4; to me the coolness behind the Tiers system is that you can have your hunters as the underdogs and your Hunters as the top dogs in the same game. I like the idea that a Tier 1 Cell might use compromise and attrition to deal with a single vampire. TF:V might just blow up an entire Elysium from a safe distance with long range hellfire missiles. (Obviously TF:V is still an underdog when compared to any Rank 6+ Spirit).<br /> <br /> I'm also not sold on number two. I mean I love mythology and since religion/myth is already a major element of Hunter so I'd be ok with including a lot more &quot;bigger things&quot;, but I think that agnostic cults could easily coincide with those who worship active interventionist deities. The foie gras cult in Hunter core for example.<br /> <br /> <br /> I guess my follow up question to you, then, would be what monsters could you see that is both scalable enough to work at every Tier and diverse enough to keep hunter's tagline of letting you play humans vs any other WoD gameline? I think a lot of the reason I latched onto Cults as the name for a chronicles book is that I can't think of anything else that would satisfy those two points. Can you think of something or a reason why those aren't as important as I think?<br /> <br /> The only other thing I can think of is to not name the Hunter book after a particular kind of monster. Mage is named after The Fallen World after all. One of the other reasons I liked Cults as a focus is that focusing on an organisation would also be usable for Hunters - I do feel Hunter needs more support for playing as part of a well oiled conspiracy, rather than an independent cell with Endowments; that stuff could separated out from the stuff about antagonistic cults. What do you you think?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=87370#post87370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7) Cults tend to have an &quot;othering&quot; element to them. It's one of my big gripes with Lovecraft. While I don't think it'd be a huge problem with my writers, I think it'd be an easy thing to fall back on. I don't want to see another WoD: Gypsies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could I ask you to expand on this point. Whether it's a chronicles book or more of a Slasher analogue, I do intend to continue with the Cults supplement I'm working on and obviously I don't want it to be a WoD: Gypsies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 03-09-2014, 08:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T09:10:59-07:00","id":87517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=87263#post87263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One thing all the Chronicle books is doing is highlighting various places around the world, and how the game might come into play there. If we ever did a Hunter book, it'd have a similar section.<br /> <br /> A thing worth noting is, if you liked Tokyo in Blood &amp; Smoke, I recently got greenlit to include a Tokyo section in Idigam Chronicle and Fallen World Chronicle. If I get my way, I'm going to turn it into a sort of cosmopolitan setting book like Chicago, spread over the various Chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh David, you always know how to get me all hot...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T08:01:37-07:00","id":88166,"title":"","content":"Will each conspiracy be receiving a new endowment to deal with these different supernatural types?<br /> <br /> And, any way we could possibly get a preview on some of them? XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2441-rez960","name":"rez960","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T08:07:51-07:00","id":88171,"title":"","content":"Will the book discuss the possibility of alliances with the monsters? Will there be GMC fleshed out versions of minor compacts like the Talbot Group?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T08:58:19-07:00","id":88205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rez960</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=88166#post88166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will each conspiracy be receiving a new endowment to deal with these different supernatural types?<br /> <br /> And, any way we could possibly get a preview on some of them? XD</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two new Compacts, two new Conspiracies. The Conspiracies both have new Endowments. <br /> <br /> I've already posted one of the Conspiracies. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/hunter-the-vigil-the-faithful-of-shulpae/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/hunter-the-vigil-the-faithful-of-shulpae/\" target=\"_blank\"> Hunter the Vigil: The Faithful of Shulpae &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/hunter-the-vigil-the-faithful-of-shulpae/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/hunter-the-vigil-the-faithful-of-shulpae/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T09:00:08-07:00","id":88206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bwgustaf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=88171#post88171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will the book discuss the possibility of alliances with the monsters? Will there be GMC fleshed out versions of minor compacts like the Talbot Group?</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of alliances comes up from time to time. <br /> <br /> No, I didn't have space to fuss with the non-core Compacts and Conspiracies. I would have loved to, but that would have eaten a ton of wordcount, and would have required readers to have at least four other supplements to use the book fully, not to mention World of Darkness, Hunter the Vigil, and the God-Machine Chronicle rules revisions. It would have been clunky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T09:06:30-07:00","id":88217,"title":"","content":"That I saw. What I meant to ask was whether or not the originals, TFV, Cheiron, Lucifuge etc etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2441-rez960","name":"rez960","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T09:32:03-07:00","id":88232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=87370#post87370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) I think monsters serve as a really good anchoring point for &quot;what is a monster, and what is human?&quot; debates. When hunters default to hunting clear monsters, that gives them a strong foundation that justifies what they do. But then when they move into other territory as an exception, they have to reconcile that as an exception, handling each as a case-by-case situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The ghouls from the core book fiction might be a good choice. They're already part of Hunter's existing material, they're not heavily tied to other games, though they <i>could</i> be compared to several: vampires because they feed on humans, werewolves because they breed with humans to reproduce, mages and mummies because they smack of old and secretive occultism, sineaters because they smack of death. They have fairly comprehensible motives that aren't too far removed from monstrous versions of basic human drives. Their level organisation is easy to scale; their level of occult interest and power outside their ghoulishness can just as easily scale. They tend to have involved humans around, making for moral dilemmas if that's your preference - but they themselves are gross enough to make ignoring dilemmas easy if <i>that's</i> your preference - and the aforementioned involved humans range easily from victims in need of rescue to sinister accomplices.<br /> <br /> I won't deny that most of this goes for most monsters, but the ghouls do seem like a bit of a perfect storm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T10:27:20-07:00","id":88273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rez960</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=88217#post88217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That I saw. What I meant to ask was whether or not the originals, TFV, Cheiron, Lucifuge etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! Yeah, there's a few new Endowments here and there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T10:28:22-07:00","id":88274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=88232#post88232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ghouls from the core book fiction might be a good choice. They're already part of Hunter's existing material, they're not heavily tied to other games, though they <i>could</i> be compared to several: vampires because they feed on humans, werewolves because they breed with humans to reproduce, mages and mummies because they smack of old and secretive occultism, sineaters because they smack of death. They have fairly comprehensible motives that aren't too far removed from monstrous versions of basic human drives. Their level organisation is easy to scale; their level of occult interest and power outside their ghoulishness can just as easily scale. They tend to have involved humans around, making for moral dilemmas if that's your preference - but they themselves are gross enough to make ignoring dilemmas easy if <i>that's</i> your preference - and the aforementioned involved humans range easily from victims in need of rescue to sinister accomplices.<br /> <br /> I won't deny that most of this goes for most monsters, but the ghouls do seem like a bit of a perfect storm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree. That'd be a good place to look. I would definitely consider them as a viable pitch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T11:41:45-07:00","id":88324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=88274#post88274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't disagree. That'd be a good place to look. I would definitely consider them as a viable pitch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hands down, I'd LOVE to see more done with the ghouls. They're such a fascinating antagonist that doesn't really tie into any other book, as SunlessNick said, and they were one of the things that got me hooked into the core fiction. They're one of the main reasons why, in a lot of my unused and unwritten Hunter game ideas, Gabreski's Boys are main NPCs or recurring protagonists/antagonists/anti-protagonists (?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T12:14:58-07:00","id":88347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=88232#post88232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ghouls from the core book fiction might be a good choice. They're already part of Hunter's existing material, they're not heavily tied to other games, though they <i>could</i> be compared to several: vampires because they feed on humans, werewolves because they breed with humans to reproduce, mages and mummies because they smack of old and secretive occultism, sineaters because they smack of death. They have fairly comprehensible motives that aren't too far removed from monstrous versions of basic human drives. Their level organisation is easy to scale; their level of occult interest and power outside their ghoulishness can just as easily scale. They tend to have involved humans around, making for moral dilemmas if that's your preference - but they themselves are gross enough to make ignoring dilemmas easy if <i>that's</i> your preference - and the aforementioned involved humans range easily from victims in need of rescue to sinister accomplices.<br /> <br /> I won't deny that most of this goes for most monsters, but the ghouls do seem like a bit of a perfect storm.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a good pitch, my only (rather big) concern is how it would affect groups like the MM with a specific focus on a different monster, or the Canites who only care about one single type of monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T13:15:46-07:00","id":88385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=88347#post88347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a good pitch, my only (rather big) concern is how it would affect groups like the MM with a specific focus on a different monster, or the Canites who only care about one single type of monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually one my biggest points of contention with considering such a book. But I have an idea percolating. Less signature monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T13:19:28-07:00","id":88387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=88385#post88385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Less signature monster.</div> </div> </div> </div> That sounds like something we can agree on <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I look forward to hearing it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T13:26:15-07:00","id":88391,"title":"","content":"I honestly feel like the &quot;Threats Unknown&quot; idea would be better for a Hunter Chronicle. Not to say Ghouls or Cults don't make good antagonists for Hunters, but...maybe a broader &quot;servants&quot; category would be more fitting as a generic way of modeling those under the command of the unknown threats that Hunters face. After that, the ST can decide the specifics so that they're really ghouls, cultists, stigmatics, or something else entirely that's using your fellow man as tools for various nefarious schemes. The servants provide more internal conflict as Hunters work out what to do, if these servants can or should be freed, while the unknown threats are the more external conflicts that the Hunters prefer, even if they are hard to put down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/671-the-lone-gunman","name":"The Lone Gunman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T14:31:16-07:00","id":88420,"title":"","content":"My thing with the potential Chronicle books is a focus less on a specific foe and more on the central themes. The Strix work well for Vampire because they're the struggle with the Beast incarnate, and ratchet up the inherent paranoia in a Requiem chronicle to 11. Having a delicious new baddie is worth a lot less than refining each game into the best it can be - the Fallen World Chronicle is promising, and the talk of a Promethean &quot;Pilgrimage Chronicle&quot; or a Geist &quot;Krewe Chronicle&quot; are much more appetizing than a big threat like the Idigam, in my eyes - and I can only hope Hunter could see the same treatment.<br /> <br /> That's not to say a big book of new monsters (<i>Threats Unknown</i> would be an instant buy for me) wouldn't be welcome, but I think a potential new core should focus much more on the cell/compact/conspiracy and how the Vigil impacts the lives of those that carry it. Good luck with a snappy name for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T14:45:46-07:00","id":88432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=88420#post88420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a Geist &quot;Krewe Chronicle&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> I should finish that some time, but I have so many more interesting projects than writing a ton of powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=88420#post88420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not to say a big book of new monsters (<i>Threats Unknown</i> would be an instant buy for me) wouldn't be welcome, but I think a potential new core should focus much more on the cell/compact/conspiracy and how the Vigil impacts the lives of those that carry it. Good luck with a snappy name for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T14:49:52-07:00","id":88435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=88420#post88420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thing with the potential Chronicle books is a focus less on a specific foe and more on the central themes. The Strix work well for Vampire because they're the struggle with the Beast incarnate, and ratchet up the inherent paranoia in a Requiem chronicle to 11. Having a delicious new baddie is worth a lot less than refining each game into the best it can be - the Fallen World Chronicle is promising, and the talk of a Promethean &quot;Pilgrimage Chronicle&quot; or a Geist &quot;Krewe Chronicle&quot; are much more appetizing than a big threat like the Idigam, in my eyes - and I can only hope Hunter could see the same treatment.<br /> <br /> That's not to say a big book of new monsters (<i>Threats Unknown</i> would be an instant buy for me) wouldn't be welcome, but I think a potential new core should focus much more on the cell/compact/conspiracy and how the Vigil impacts the lives of those that carry it. Good luck with a snappy name for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Undying Wick&quot;? &quot;The Unending Watch&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T15:52:06-07:00","id":88474,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Dudes Who Are Like Tiny Lights In A World of Darkness&quot; Chronicle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T16:42:07-07:00","id":88495,"title":"","content":"Freelance Police Chronicle.<br /> <br /> Just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T16:47:37-07:00","id":88496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=88495#post88495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Freelance Police Chronicle.<br /> <br /> Just saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>...That is an amazing idea.<br /> <br /> MachineIV, could this be tied into the ghoul idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T17:05:39-07:00","id":88506,"title":"","content":"While we're at all this; fingers crossed for a Chronicle book to make VASCU core and fix the Ascending Ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T17:43:01-07:00","id":88523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=86680#post86680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Updated rules for risking Willpower.<br /> <br /> Couple of notes on Dread Powers.<br /> <br /> I added a section on creating monsters, it's pretty rough but offers some ideas and advice.<br /> <br /> Then I offer some loose creation rules for less important and more important monsters (so you don't need to fully stat every mook).<br /> <br /> There's some guidelines for creating new monster templates whole cloth.</div> </div> </div> </div>You sir, are both a mindreader and my hero.<br /> <br /> SHUDDUP AND TAKE MY MONEY!!!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/568-viperion","name":"Viperion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar568_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T00:33:55-07:00","id":88702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84923-htv-mortal-remains?p=88506#post88506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While we're at all this; fingers crossed for a Chronicle book to make VASCU core and fix the Ascending Ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do the Ascending Ones need fixing? They're great. They just need a better organisation structure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"k